agent-ops task task-2fda8c33-80c8-41ae-9a44-a22563dca6af: Opt-in run profile: route >5-criteria changes to agent-ops run
intent: Add installation profile `run` (capability `auto-run`, pulls in core+loop). With it, Claude Code and Codex managed rules tell the agent to hand changes needing more than five acceptance criteria to `agent-ops run` (goal file .agent-ops/state/run-goal.md, --host claude|codex, --wait, Codex escalated like review), relay questions via run respond, fall back to subtask flow on RUN_TARGET_REQUIRED/RUN_BACKGROUND_UNSUPPORTED/RUN_TARGET_DIRTY/WORKTREE_NESTED, stop and ask on RUN_REPO_UNTRUSTED, and report status/logs/resume/stop commands on non-completion. agy text and all outputs without auto-run stay byte-identical. Pre-authorize `agent-ops run` for Claude and Codex with the profile. The Claude PreToolUse worktree hook allows a write to exactly .agent-ops/state/run-goal.md in the main checkout without creating a worktree when auto-run is active. Document in README, docs/en/spec and docs/zh-TW/spec.
criteria:
- profile-and-preauth: schemas/config.schema.json accepts "run" in profiles; resolveProfiles(["run"]) yields core, loop, run with capability auto-run; with the run profile Claude preauth includes Bash(agent-ops run *) and Codex preauth includes rules for `agent-ops run` and `agent-ops run *` with an escalation justification, and without it preauth is unchanged. Unit tests in npm test.
- managed-rules-text: managedRules for Claude Code and Codex descriptors with auto-run carry the >5-criteria threshold, host flag, goal-file hand-off before task create, background wait and run respond relay, start-refusal fallback (RUN_TARGET_REQUIRED, RUN_BACKGROUND_UNSUPPORTED, RUN_TARGET_DIRTY, WORKTREE_NESTED) and RUN_REPO_UNTRUSTED stop, and non-completion reporting with run resume/stop commands; Codex text carries the escalated invocation; agy output and every output without auto-run are byte-identical to before (snapshot test). Unit tests in npm test.
- goal-file-write-exemption: With auto-run and worktree.mode auto, the Claude PreToolUse hook allows a write to exactly .agent-ops/state/run-goal.md in the main checkout and creates no worktree; any other main-checkout write still yields WORKTREE_CREATED, and without auto-run the goal-file write still yields WORKTREE_CREATED. Unit test in npm test.
- docs: README, docs/en/spec and the docs/zh-TW/spec mirror document the run profile, its >5-criteria threshold, fallback on start refusal, and failure handling; any existing docs-consistency tests in npm test pass.
- suite-package-scan: npm test passes in full; npm run package:check and the source scan also pass on the final commit.
